You must include one or more code statements in point 1 and 2.
Code statements included in point 1 should be as brief as possible, only include the ones that are most related to the root cause and  the number of code statements may not exceed 3.


Here is the commit message:
SOLR-4218: SolrTestCaseJ4 throws NPE when closing the core
 (on the afterClass method)

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1423932 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug is caused by the `HttpShardHandlerFactory` attempting to call the `shutdown` method on `defaultClient` and `loadbalancer` without checking if these objects are null. If either object is null, this results in a NullPointerException (NPE) when the core is being closed in the `afterClass` method of `SolrTestCaseJ4`.

Here is the patch:

   @Override
   public void close() {
     try {
       ExecutorUtil.shutdownAndAwaitTermination(commExecutor);
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }

     try {
-      defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
+      if(defaultClient != null) {
+        defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
+      }
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }
     try {
-      loadbalancer.shutdown();
+      if(loadbalancer != null) {
+        loadbalancer.shutdown();
+      }
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }

   }
 }


